<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d1" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="T01. Artificial Intelligence will improve society more than it will create problems." />
    <node id="T02. Generative AI tools should be allowed as learning aids in higher education." />
    <node id="T03. Students should disclose the use of AI in assignments and reports." />
    <node id="T04. Every engineering student should receive formal education in AI." />
    <node id="T05. Artificial Intelligence will significantly accelerate scientific discovery." />
    <node id="T06. Most repetitive jobs will eventually be replaced by intelligent automation." />
    <node id="T07. Robots should replace humans in hazardous occupations whenever possible." />
    <node id="T08. AI-assisted diagnosis should become routine in healthcare." />
    <node id="T09. Autonomous vehicles will ultimately make transportation safer." />
    <node id="T10. Protection of personal data is more important than technological convenience." />
    <node id="T11. Technology companies should explain how recommendation algorithms work." />
    <node id="T12. Governments should introduce stricter regulations for Artificial Intelligence." />
    <node id="T13. Cybersecurity deserves greater investment than the development of new digital technologies." />
    <node id="T14. Social media algorithms contribute to opinion polarization." />
    <node id="T15. Society will increasingly depend on AI-assisted decision making." />
    <node id="E01. Project-based learning develops deeper understanding than examination-oriented learning." />
    <node id="E02. Traditional written examinations accurately measure a student's knowledge." />
    <node id="E03. Class attendance should be compulsory for all courses." />
    <node id="E04. High-quality online learning can effectively complement classroom teaching." />
    <node id="E05. Students should be encouraged to take courses outside their primary discipline." />
    <node id="E06. Every undergraduate student should participate in at least one research project." />
    <node id="E07. Publishing research before graduation should be encouraged, but not mandatory." />
    <node id="E08. Maintaining academic honesty is more important than obtaining high grades." />
    <node id="E09. Collaborative learning is generally more effective than individual learning." />
    <node id="E10. Universities should prioritize innovation and problem-solving over rote learning." />
    <node id="E11. University curricula should be updated more frequently to match emerging technologies." />
    <node id="E12. Artificial intelligence should be integrated into teaching and personalized learning." />
    <node id="E13. Universities should invest more resources in research than in expanding infrastructure." />
    <node id="E14. Strong collaborations between universities and industry improve student education." />
    <node id="E15. Continuous learning and skill development are essential throughout one's career." />
    <node id="S01. Every individual has a responsibility to contribute positively to society." />
    <node id="S02. Universities should encourage students to participate in community service activities." />
    <node id="S03. New technologies should be evaluated for their societal impact before widespread deployment." />
    <node id="S04. Technology companies should be accountable for unethical use of their platforms." />
    <node id="S05. Individuals should have greater control over how their personal data are collected and used." />
    <node id="S06. Combating online misinformation requires shared responsibility among users, platforms, and governments." />
    <node id="S07. Equal opportunities should be prioritized regardless of a person's background." />
    <node id="S08. Diverse teams generally make better decisions than homogeneous teams." />
    <node id="S09. Universities should promote an inclusive environment where different viewpoints can be discussed respectfully." />
    <node id="S10. Scientific evidence should play an important role in public policy decisions." />
    <node id="S11. People should be free to express differing opinions as long as they do not promote harm or discrimination." />
    <node id="S12. Young people should actively participate in addressing societal challenges." />
    <node id="S13. Critical evaluation of online information should be taught as a core educational skill." />
    <node id="S14. Leaders should prioritize ethical decision-making even when it reduces short-term gains." />
    <node id="S15. Building public trust is essential for responsible adoption of emerging technologies." />
    <node id="V01. Climate change requires immediate global action." />
    <node id="V02. Governments should prioritize investment in renewable energy over fossil fuels." />
    <node id="V03. Individuals should actively reduce their personal energy consumption." />
    <node id="V04. Public transportation and non-motorized transport should be promoted even if they require additional public investment." />
    <node id="V05. Single-use plastics should be significantly restricted." />
    <node id="V06. Water conservation should be a priority in households, institutions, and industries." />
    <node id="V07. Protecting biodiversity is essential for long-term human well-being." />
    <node id="V08. Universities should adopt environmentally sustainable campus practices even if implementation costs increase." />
    <node id="V09. Products should be designed to encourage reuse, repair, and recycling." />
    <node id="V10. Consumers should consider environmental impact when purchasing products." />
    <node id="V11. Technological innovation is essential for addressing environmental challenges." />
    <node id="V12. Environmental sustainability should be integrated into higher education curricula." />
    <node id="V13. Companies should be held accountable for the environmental impacts of their activities." />
    <node id="V14. International cooperation is necessary to effectively address environmental challenges." />
    <node id="V15. Current generations have a responsibility to protect natural resources for future generations." />
